The solution is correct. Completing the square gives (n+7)² − k² = 1404, so (n+7−k)(n+7+k) = 1404 with both factors even (same parity, product even). With 1404 = 4·351, the factor pairs (2d, 2·351/d) for divisors d ≤ √351 yield n = 345, 113, 41, all verified to give perfect squares. Sum = 499.

Note: n positive excludes any further restrictions — all three solutions are positive, and there are no missing cases (a, b must both be even since 1404 ≡ 0 mod 4... actually just even, which the 2d parametrization captures since 1404 = 4·351). The three solutions check out and sum to 499.

