The setup is correct: (n+7-k)(n+7+k)=1404, ab=351, n=a+b-7. However, the factorization 351 = 27 × 13 = 3³ × 13 gives **four** factor pairs: (1,351), (3,117), (9,39), and also **(13,27)**. The proposed answer missed the pair (13,27), which gives n = 13+27-7 = 33, k = 14. Verify: 33² + 14(33) - 1355 = 1089 + 462 - 1355 = 196 = 14². ✓

So the valid n values are 345, 113, 41, and 33, summing to 532.

